description:
Now you know else, and if. You may be thniking "What else could their be?" The answer? `else if`. Else If is just another if statement if the if statment does not execute. ```
if(thing)
{
    code
}
else if(thing)
{
    code
}
```
is equivilant to 
```
if (thing)
{
    code
}
else
{
    if (thing) { 
        code
    }
}
```
. Way shorter, right?
---
## Assignment:
The Chronoshard team is having a issue! If the player is dying and dead, then it prints both messages! Fix it using a else if statement.

starterCode:
using System;

namespace Chronoshard.Core
{
    class Program
    {
        public static int Main(string[] args)
        {
            bool is_dying = true;
            bool is_dead = true;
            if (is_dead)
                {
                Console.WriteLine("You have died");
            }
            if (is_dying)
                {
                Console.WriteLine("You're dying");
            }
            else
                {
                Console.WriteLine("You are OK");
            }
            // Don't touch below this line.
            return 0;
        }
    }
}
